gocode third-party notices
==========================

gocode bundles the following third-party software in its release binaries.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ugrep
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Project:   https://github.com/Genivia/ugrep
Version:   see third_party/ugrep/VERSION (also printed by
           `gocode --version --verbose`)
Copyright: (c) 2023, Robert van Engelen, Genivia Inc.
License:   BSD 3-Clause License
Files:     third_party/ugrep/LICENSE.txt
Checksums: third_party/ugrep/checksums.txt

gocode embeds a ugrep binary (`ugrep` / `ugrep.exe`) for the platforms listed
in third_party/ugrep/checksums.txt: either the unmodified official release
binary, verified against the sha256 published with the upstream release, or a
build of the tagged upstream source (see third_party/ugrep/UPDATING.md). At
runtime it is written to the user cache directory
(<cache>/gocode/ugrep/<version>/) and re-verified before use. gocode never
downloads ugrep at runtime.

The official Windows release binary statically includes these libraries; their
licence texts are in third_party/ugrep/licenses/:

  PCRE2        BSD 3-Clause with the PCRE2 exception   PCRE2-LICENCE.md
  zlib         zlib License                            zlib-LICENSE
  bzip2        bzip2 License (BSD-style)               bzip2-LICENSE
  XZ (liblzma) BSD Zero Clause License                 xz-COPYING.0BSD
  LZ4          BSD 2-Clause                            lz4-LICENSE
  Zstandard    BSD 3-Clause                            zstd-LICENSE

Binaries built from source with scripts/fetch-ugrep.sh --build statically
include PCRE2 only.

